# Local HolyC scratch (historically created by older make test targets)
tests/simple.hc

# Accidental root/test dump binaries (sources live under tests/scratch/)
/test_*
# Same prefixes elsewhere (harness leftovers)
test_*
!test_*.hc
!test_*.sh
!tests/scratch/**/*.hc
dump_*
trace_*
# Local scratch-script names, deliberately unanchored because the scratch turns up anywhere.
# They used to swallow docs/DEBUG_STATE_SURVEY.md — case-insensitively, as this filesystem is
# — and hid it for a whole session: an ignored file is not untracked, so git add said nothing
# and git status showed nothing while several commits claimed to add it. Hence the docs/
# exemption, which must stay AFTER these and BEFORE the docs/archive/ rule below.
verify_*
show_*
debug_*
check_*
analyze_*
!docs/**
# ...and tests/scripts/, for the same reason docs/ is exempt. It holds 151 TRACKED gate
# scripts, not scratch, and `check_*` had silently swallowed two that the Makefile depends on:
# check_no_debug_probes.sh (Makefile:66) and check_asm_catalog.py (Makefile:724). Both were
# untracked for who knows how long, so a fresh clone could not run either gate while every
# local run passed. An ignored file is not untracked: `git add` says nothing and `git status`
# shows nothing, which is exactly how docs/DEBUG_STATE_SURVEY.md went missing above.
!tests/scripts/**
# ...and tools/, third time. It holds TRACKED tooling, not scratch, and `check_*` swallowed
# tools/check_prj_collisions.py the day it was written — `git add` refused and said so, which is
# only luckier than the two silent cases above. Same reasoning, same fix.
!tools/**
# The one build artifact in tools/, by EXACT PATH (Makefile `clean` removes it).
tools/pack_tosb
# The two genuine scratch scripts in there, by EXACT PATH. Named individually on purpose: a
# glob here is what hid the gates above, and an exact path cannot swallow a file nobody has
# written yet.
tests/scripts/analyze_source_tree.sh
tests/scripts/trace_add_call.sh

